.TH "DEDALUS" "1" "" "dedalus" "Dedalus Manual"
.SH "NAME"
dedalus \- command line interface for the Dedalus REST API
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.B dedalus
[\fIglobal options\fR] \fIcommand\fR [\fIsubcommand\fR] [\fIarguments\fR] [\fIoptions\fR]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
dedalus calls the Dedalus REST API from the command line. Commands are grouped by resource, and every command prints its result to standard output in the configured format.
.PP
Controlplane API for Dedalus Cloud Services (DCS).
.SH "GLOBAL OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-\-base\-url\fR \fI<url>\fR
Override the base URL for API requests.
.TP
\fB\-\-timeout\fR \fI<ms>\fR
Request timeout in milliseconds.
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-retries\fR \fI<count>\fR
Number of retries for retryable failures.
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fI<format>\fR
Output format: auto, json, jsonl, pretty, raw, toon, yaml.
.TP
\fB\-\-format\-error\fR \fI<format>\fR
Error output format: auto, json, jsonl, pretty, raw, toon, yaml.
.TP
\fB\-\-transform\fR \fI<path>\fR
Dot\-path transform for data output.
.TP
\fB\-\-transform\-error\fR \fI<path>\fR
Dot\-path transform for error output.
.TP
\fB\-r\fR, \fB\-\-raw\-output\fR
Print transformed string values without JSON quotes.
.TP
\fB\-\-debug\fR
Enable SDK debug logging on standard error.
.TP
\fB\-\-api\-key\fR \fI<value>\fR
Dedalus API key or short\-lived delegated access token in Authorization: Bearer <credential>. Can also be set with the DEDALUS_API_KEY environment variable.
.TP
\fB\-\-x\-api\-key\fR \fI<value>\fR
Dedalus API key. Alternative to Bearer token. Can also be set with the DEDALUS_X_API_KEY environment variable.
.SH "COMMANDS"
.TP
\fBdedalus machines list\fR
List machines. See dedalus\-machines\-list(1).
.TP
\fBdedalus machines create\fR
Create machine. See dedalus\-machines\-create(1).
.TP
\fBdedalus machines retrieve\fR
Get machine. See dedalus\-machines\-retrieve(1).
.TP
\fBdedalus machines update\fR
Update machine. See dedalus\-machines\-update(1).
.TP
\fBdedalus machines delete\fR
Destroy machine. See dedalus\-machines\-delete(1).
.TP
\fBdedalus machines sleep\fR
Sleep a running machine. See dedalus\-machines\-sleep(1).
.TP
\fBdedalus machines wake\fR
Wake a sleeping machine. See dedalus\-machines\-wake(1).
.TP
\fBdedalus machines reboot\fR
Reboot a machine with fresh memory. See dedalus\-machines\-reboot(1).
.TP
\fBdedalus machines:ssh list\fR
List SSH sessions. See dedalus\-machines\-ssh\-list(1).
.TP
\fBdedalus machines:ssh create\fR
Create SSH session. See dedalus\-machines\-ssh\-create(1).
.TP
\fBdedalus machines:ssh retrieve\fR
Get SSH session. See dedalus\-machines\-ssh\-retrieve(1).
.TP
\fBdedalus machines:ssh delete\fR
Delete SSH session. See dedalus\-machines\-ssh\-delete(1).
.TP
\fBdedalus machines:executions list\fR
List executions. See dedalus\-machines\-executions\-list(1).
.TP
\fBdedalus machines:executions create\fR
Create execution. See dedalus\-machines\-executions\-create(1).
.TP
\fBdedalus machines:executions retrieve\fR
Get execution. See dedalus\-machines\-executions\-retrieve(1).
.TP
\fBdedalus machines:executions delete\fR
Delete execution. See dedalus\-machines\-executions\-delete(1).
.TP
\fBdedalus machines:executions output\fR
Get execution output. See dedalus\-machines\-executions\-output(1).
.TP
\fBdedalus machines:executions events\fR
List execution events. See dedalus\-machines\-executions\-events(1).
.TP
\fBdedalus machines:executions:logs retrieve\fR
Get execution log status. See dedalus\-machines\-executions\-logs\-retrieve(1).
.TP
\fBdedalus machines:executions:logs reauthorize\fR
Reauthorize execution log publication. See dedalus\-machines\-executions\-logs\-reauthorize(1).
.TP
\fBdedalus machines:executions:logs create\-token\fR
Create execution log read token. See dedalus\-machines\-executions\-logs\-create\-token(1).
.TP
\fBdedalus machines:autoresizing retrieve\fR
Read this machine's RAM autoresizing settings. See dedalus\-machines\-autoresizing\-retrieve(1).
.TP
\fBdedalus machines:autoresizing update\fR
Set this machine's RAM autoresizing settings. See dedalus\-machines\-autoresizing\-update(1).
.TP
\fBdedalus organization:autoresizing retrieve\fR
Read organization RAM autoresizing policy. See dedalus\-organization\-autoresizing\-retrieve(1).
.TP
\fBdedalus organization:autoresizing update\fR
Set organization RAM autoresizing policy. See dedalus\-organization\-autoresizing\-update(1).
.TP
\fBdedalus completion\fR
Print a shell completion script. See dedalus\-completion(1).
.TP
\fBdedalus login\fR
Sign in and save credentials for later commands. See dedalus\-login(1).
.TP
\fBdedalus logout\fR
Forget saved credentials. See dedalus\-logout(1).
.SH "FILE ARGUMENTS"
Any command flag or credential reads its value from a file when the value begins with @. A flag shown with a <path> value uploads a file and takes its path with or without the @. The global options above are read exactly as written.
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
dedalus COMMAND \-\-FLAG @./body.json    # contents of the file
dedalus COMMAND \-\-FLAG @file://./n.txt # always sent as text
dedalus COMMAND \-\-FLAG @data://./l.png # always base64\-encoded
dedalus COMMAND \-\-FLAG '\e@literal'    # a value that begins with @
.fi
.RE
.SH "SHELL COMPLETION"
dedalus completion <shell> prints a completion script for bash, zsh, and fish. Load it from your shell startup file:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
eval "$(dedalus completion bash)"
eval "$(dedalus completion zsh)"
dedalus completion fish | source
.fi
.RE
.SH "ENVIRONMENT"
.TP
\fBDEDALUS_API_KEY\fR
Fallback for \-\-api\-key when the flag is not passed.
.TP
\fBDEDALUS_X_API_KEY\fR
Fallback for \-\-x\-api\-key when the flag is not passed.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
\fB0\fR
The command completed successfully.
.TP
\fB1\fR
The request failed for an unclassified reason. Reported as error.
.TP
\fB2\fR
The command was invoked incorrectly (missing or invalid arguments).
.TP
\fB10\fR
Authentication or authorization failed (HTTP 401 or 403). Reported as auth\-failed.
.TP
\fB11\fR
The requested resource does not exist (HTTP 404). Reported as not\-found.
.TP
\fB12\fR
The request was rate limited (HTTP 429). Reported as rate\-limited.
.TP
\fB13\fR
The request was rejected (any other HTTP 4xx). Reported as client\-error.
.TP
\fB14\fR
The API failed to handle the request (HTTP 5xx). Reported as server\-error.
.TP
\fB15\fR
The API could not be reached, or the request timed out. Reported as connection\-error.
